  "notes": "{抜|ぬ}ける is an intransitive ichidan verb with multiple meanings: to come out, be missing, or pass through.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- {自動詞|じどうし}: {抜|ぬ}ける (to come out/fall out)\n- {他動詞|たどうし}: {抜|ぬ}く (to pull out)\n\nIDIOMS:\n- {気|き}が{抜|ぬ}ける: to feel deflated/let down\n- {腰|こし}が{抜|ぬ}ける: legs give way (from shock)\n- {魂|たましい}が{抜|ぬ}ける: to be dazed\n\nCOMMON USES:\n- {髪|かみ}の{毛|け}が{抜|ぬ}ける: hair falls out\n- トンネルを{抜|ぬ}ける: to pass through a tunnel\n- {名前|なまえ}が{抜|ぬ}けている: a name is missing",
